# Env and Secrets

## Source of truth
- Infisical environments drive deploy exports to `.env.infisical`
- Config validated via Zod schemas in `libs/config`

## Rules
- Never commit real secrets, private keys, VAPID keys, SMTP tokens, or DB passwords
- Do not log env values or JWT material (avoid `/tmp` debug dumps)
- New env vars: add Zod schema + document in ops docs/examples; fail closed in production
- Prefer RSA JWT key env vars for HTTP auth; treat legacy HMAC secrets as legacy-only
- Migration credentials stay out of runtime service env
- Compose/k3s must not embed plaintext secrets in tracked manifests — reference secret stores
- If a secret may have been committed historically, rotate it; do not "fix" by only deleting the file
